    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="9db2b854-5f5e-5710-8294-06881ea9ecaf" activityNameId="d1b5c10c-ff55-59ae-8d43-ef6f6f46eeb4" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Phosphorous pentachloride, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Phosphorous pentachloride, at plant
The dataset can be used for example as base material in the production of LiPF6. Data are based on patents. ;
CAS number: 010026-13-8; 
Formula: PCl5; 
Synonyms: Phosphor(V)-chlorid; 
UUID: ed2c67ce-6029-3d6f-96dd-cc5fed4a5e07
This dataset includes the reaction of phosporous trichloride with chlorine to phosphorous pentachloride in an autoclave with a reaction temperatur at 180-210°C and under pressure. Energy consumption, chlorine and phosphorous trichloride emissions to air are calculated. For infrastructure, the ecoinvent dataset "chemical plant, organics" is accounted. Transportation efforts are based on ecoinvent standard estimates.
Location: Some European datasets are used for global processes.
Technology: This dataset includes a method of producing phosphorous pentachloride out of phosphorous trichloride and chlorine. Temperature in the autoclave reactor: 180 - 220 °C; pressure: 5-6 bar. PCL3 conversion is 93.9%. 
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: patent, ecoinvent 
Extrapolations: see Geography
Uncertainty adjustments: Uncertainty is assessed using the pedigree matrix.
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_ed2c67ce-6029-3d6f-96dd-cc5fed4a5e07.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
